-- title:
--   Finite program for deterministic unequal-tolerance signing
-- statement:
--   This is the fixed 746-instruction deterministic signing program of Section 4. Its integer header gives the input dimension, row count and number of tests; real arrays hold the unit vectors and their individual tolerances. Its outputs are the sign matrix and the normalized projection matrix, with every normalization operation charged. For each test and each potential sign, it maintains $p,a,M,T,J,R,\Psi$ and updates
--
--   $$R=(MJ)^{-1/2}\exp(\alpha p^2/J-\alpha a).$$
--
--   The program builds coordinate-specific affected-test lists, maintains total candidate potentials, fixes entries by row then column, and chooses $+1$ on an equal-potential tie. A row is initialized once when it becomes active; unchanged rows are represented by the maintained potential product. All scalar updates are equations (27)–(32), evaluated by arithmetic, square root and exponential instructions. This is executable code without any guarantee bundled into its input or output.
-- source:
--   Vladimir Braverman, Kuan Cheng, Jiaqing Zhu, STOC 2027 submission #1373 (October 2026), pp. 15–18, Lemma 4.5, equations (27)–(32); https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/1373.pdf

